# The company's own staff at the jump host of one site (plant/sites.yaml, `staff`;
# docs/multisite/PLANS.md 4.6), each with a named account instead of a shared login.
# No node injects this file. plantgen writes a site's copy with that site's roster
# (plant/generated/fleet/<code>/injects/guacamole/staff.env), and the site's
# topology injects the copy, mode 0600, into two nodes:
#   dmz-jump   cm_staff_sql.py creates each person's Guacamole account, TOTP key,
#              and own copies of the EWS connections
#   ews        71-ews-staff.sh creates each person's local EWS account
# so the two always agree.
#
# The values of a copy are a fallback only: the cherrymountain app renders the file
# per experiment (new passwords and TOTP keys) and its injection replaces the copy
# on both nodes. They are used only when the topology runs without the app, and
# protect nothing outside the range. TOTP is a standard RFC 6238 secret (SHA-1,
# 6 digits, 30 s), so any authenticator works with it; the key is in Base32 as
# Guacamole stores it.
STAFF_COUNT=0
